-- Intake compliance records stranded by the Supabase → Neon cutover.
--
-- `intake_compliance_records` is written on every intake and read by the
-- request detail's Compliance tab, but it was missing from the migration's copy
-- list. Thirty-nine rows — one per pre-cutover request — stayed in Supabase and
-- nothing reported it, which silently undid the earlier "Compliance is never
-- empty" backfill for those requests.
--
-- Exported verbatim from Supabase so the recovery needs **only Neon**: running
-- this does not require the retired project to exist, which is what lets
-- Supabase be removed entirely. Every statement is ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING, so
-- re-running is safe and a row already present is left alone.
--
--   psql "$NEON_DATABASE_URL" -f db/backfills/2026-09-02-intake-compliance-records.sql
--
-- or, without psql:
--
--   npm run backfill:intake-compliance

